      },
    },
    "/api/companion/models": {
      "get": {
        "description": "LLM model endpoints the CALLER can use.

The stock /api/models route scopes to get_current_user, which for a
bearer token is the sandboxed pseudo-user "api" (owns nothing). Here we
scope to the token's real owner instead, plus legacy null-owner shared
rows -- the same rule as owner_filter. Read-only; never returns api_key
material.",
        "operationId": "models_api_companion_models_get",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {},
              },
            },
            "description": "Successful Response",
          },
        },
        "summary": "Models",
        "tags": [
          "companion",
        ],
      },
    },
    "/api/companion/pair": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Admin-only pairing page. Renders a form that POSTs to mint a code.

A GET never mints a credential: SameSite=Lax session cookies ride
top-level GET navigations, so minting on GET would be triggerable by a
link or <img> (CSRF). The actual mint is the POST handler below.",
        "operationId": "pair_page_api_companion_pair_get",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {},
              },
            },
            "description": "Successful Response",
          },
        },
        "summary": "Pair Page",
        "tags": [
          "companion",
        ],
      },
      "post": {
        "description": "Mint a pairing code. Admin-cookie only; CSRF-safe because the
SameSite=Lax session cookie is not sent on a cross-site POST (same
protection as POST /api/tokens). Minting invalidates the token cache so
the code works immediately, no restart. \`?format=json\` returns the
payload for an in-app pairing screen.",
        "operationId": "pair_create_api_companion_pair_post",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {},
              },
            },
            "description": "Successful Response",
          },
        },
        "summary": "Pair Create",
        "tags": [
          "companion",
        ],
      },
    },
    "/api/companion/ping": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Cheap, auth-validated health check. A 200 with ok=true confirms the
host/port and credential are valid; middleware returns 401 otherwise.",
        "operationId": "ping_api_companion_ping_get",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {},
              },
            },
            "description": "Successful Response",
          },
        },
        "summary": "Ping",
        "tags": [
          "companion",
        ],
      },
    },
